"""
A non-replaced element whose UA display is `inline` must shrink-wrap to the sum
of its inline content advances (plus its own padding and border), never to the
container's content width.

CSS 2.1 §9.2.2 / §10.3.1: an inline, non-replaced box has no computed width;
its width is its content's. §10.6.1 gives its content area the font's height,
not the line box's. This renderer already implements both — the inline branch
of `layout_with_style` calls `intrinsic_text_width` (which adds the element's
own padding and border) and clamps the height with `inline_content_area_height`.

The defect was upstream of that branch and was not in the layout code at all:
`display` comes from a hardcoded UA tag table, `is_inline_tag`
(`simple_web_html_layout_renderer_style.spl`), applied at
`simple_web_html_layout_renderer_declarations.spl:1269`. Twelve phrasing-content
tags were missing from it, so each fell through to the BLOCK path, took the
container's content width, and got a line box's height. Measured against
headless Chrome (`--headless=new --window-size=900,20000`, Chrome 152) on the
`html` catalog page, the row that names the cluster:

    Chrome   path:0/0/4/2/8/1/0 | bdi | x=106 | w=86
    diff     path:0/0/4/2/8/1/0 | bdi | inline | dx=0 dy=2 dw=642 dh=6

Simple reported 728 — the `<li>`'s full content width. Ten such ROOT rows on
that page alone (`bdi`, `bdo`, `cite`, `data`, `del`, `dfn`, `ins`, `q`, `s`,
`u`), each with an inherited ladder beneath it.

The tag list added here is not read off the HTML specification: it is the set
Chrome actually reports `display=inline` for across the eight catalog pages,
minus the tags the table already carried, minus the replaced media elements
(`audio`/`video`/`canvas`), which are a different mechanism and are covered by
`replaced_element_default_intrinsic_box_spec.spl`.

SABOTAGE (run before landing): remove `tag == "bdi"` from `is_inline_tag` and
AC-1 fails at 728 while AC-3 (`<span>`, always in the table) and AC-4
(`<p>`, block, must stay 728) both still pass — so the spec is measuring the UA
table entry and not the fixture.

STATED RESIDUE, not asserted here: Chrome's UA stylesheet gives `<q>` open and
close quotation marks through `::before`/`::after`. This renderer generates no
such content, so `<q>` shrink-wraps to the right mechanism but stays about two
characters narrow. That is recorded rather than faked with hardcoded quotes.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-INLINE-006 — every tag the UA stylesheet gives `display: inline` resolves to inline, and an inline non-replaced box shrink-wraps to its content width with a font-height content area.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_style.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer_style.{
    is_inline_tag
}

val VW: i32 = 900
val VH: i32 = 20000
val HEAD: text = "<html><head><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}div{width:728px;margin:0;padding:0}</style></head><body><div>"

fn probe(inner: text, prop: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(
        HEAD + inner + "</div></body></html>", VW, VH, "x", prop)

fn wrapped(tag: text, prop: text) -> text:
    probe("<" + tag + " id=\"x\">hello</" + tag + "> tail", prop)

describe "the UA inline-tag table covers all phrasing content":
    it "AC-1: <bdi> shrink-wraps to its text, not to the 728 px container":
        step("the html-page cluster row: Chrome 86 against Simple's 728")
        expect(wrapped("bdi", "w")).to_equal("34")

    it "AC-2: an inline box's content area is the font height, not the line box":
        step("CSS 2.1 §10.6.1 — 18 px content area under a 24 px line box")
        expect(wrapped("bdi", "h")).to_equal("18")

    it "AC-3 (control): <span> was already in the table and must not move":
        step("same markup, a tag the table always carried — the reference width")
        expect(wrapped("span", "w")).to_equal("34")

    it "AC-4 (control): <p> is block and must still take the full container width":
        step("a fix that shrink-wrapped everything would break this row")
        expect(probe("<p id=\"x\">hello</p>", "w")).to_equal("728")

    it "AC-5: <bdi> and <span> agree, which is what 'same display' means":
        step("the table entry is the only difference between them")
        expect(wrapped("bdi", "w")).to_equal(wrapped("span", "w"))

    it "AC-6: every tag added this round resolves inline in the UA table":
        step("the measured Chrome display=inline set for the 8-page catalog")
        var missing = ""
        for t in ["bdi", "bdo", "cite", "data", "del", "dfn", "ins", "output", "q", "s", "u", "wbr"]:
            if not is_inline_tag(t):
                missing = missing + t + " "
        expect(missing).to_equal("")

    it "AC-7 (control): a block tag must NOT have been swept into the table":
        step("the guard against widening the table until everything is inline")
        var wrong = ""
        for t in ["p", "div", "li", "section", "ul", "table"]:
            if is_inline_tag(t):
                wrong = wrong + t + " "
        expect(wrong).to_equal("")

    it "AC-8: <bdo> and <del>, two more of the ten root rows, shrink-wrap too":
        step("one row is an anecdote; the cluster is the claim")
        expect(wrapped("bdo", "w") + "/" + wrapped("del", "w")).to_equal("34/34")
